     \[
     PQ^2 = QR^2 + PR^2 - 2 \cdot QR \cdot PR \cdot \cos(\angle PQR)
     \]
     Substituting the given values:
     \[
     100 = 100 + PR^2 - 2 \cdot 10 \cdot PR \cdot \cos(30^\circ)
